WEBVTT

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:26.000
Why didn't you follow instructions?

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Well... I freaked out
and totally forgot about them.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.450
It seems the toy was
too good for the likes of you.

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:34.910
Punish him!

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:43.160
Hey! What would happen if someone
got attacked by that many people?!

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:45.660
I'm looking forward to finding out.

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:55.330
Wait!

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:00.910
They can still be of use to us.

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:04.500
As bait to lure out the guys that got away.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.370
Very well. However, should you fail,

00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:18.450
you do realize what will happen to those
adorable children, don't you?

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:19.870
Yeah.

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:41.410
Looks like the three of us are
the only ones who can move right.

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:44.580
Still, all of us managed to escape somehow.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:48.330
I see no sign of Fling Posse, though.

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:50.450
You don't think they've been captured, do you?!

00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:53.160
Ramuda ain't the kind of
guy who'd slip up like that.

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:54.410
That's right.

00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:56.950
He certainly knows what he's doing.

00:01:56.950 --> 00:02:02.370
Anyhow, those Chuohku bitches
played us for a bunch of fools!

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:04.290
The division battle may have been

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:09.750
merely an event to select people that the
Party of Words could use for its own ends.

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:16.830
So, with these mics,
they've been makin' us dance to their tune?!

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:18.450
Samatoki...

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:20.700
But I won't get rid of this!

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:26.000
With the mic they made, I'll play hardball
and push their backs against the wall!

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.580
Hmm. That's the sort of answer
I'd expect from you, Samatoki.

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:31.950
"Tom"

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:33.870
--Tom?!
--Huh?

00:02:35.290 --> 00:02:38.160
Ichiro, is everyone with you?

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:41.830
You punks sure didn't play fair back there!

00:02:41.830 --> 00:02:44.750
I apologize about the hypnosis canceller.

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:48.910
We had no idea Chuohku
was going to use something like that.

00:02:48.910 --> 00:02:51.160
So, what do you want?

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:53.290
We want a rematch.

00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:56.200
This time it'll be a fair fight.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:58.750
And you expect us to believe that, huh?!

00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:01.580
We'll be the only ones
going to the battleground.

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:04.540
Will you give us any guarantee it's not a trap?

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:07.660
Either way, you guys can't refuse, Doctor.

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:11.330
Fling Posse is in our custody.

00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:14.790
They were caught trying to rescue you.

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:16.160
Not really.

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:20.080
It just happened while
we were making our escape.

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:22.700
Fling Posse rescued us?

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:25.450
I see. So, they were
the ones behind the blackout.

00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:28.250
So, that's why it happened
at just the right time.

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:31.000
Because of them, we...

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:34.580
That's that. I'll send you the time and place.

00:03:35.870 --> 00:03:38.870
That Amemura would do such a thing...

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:42.700
Samatoki!

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:45.250
Looks like you guys still can't move right.

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:48.250
Stay there and rest up.

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:52.370
I'll crush those bastards single-handed!

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:57.250
What's with this subway?

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:58.620
Where is it takin' us?

00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:01.660
At present, it seemeth
that we are bound for Hell.

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:05.160
This is the Prime Minister's private train
that leaves from her official residence.

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:08.250
Wow! I can't believe she has something like this.

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:09.750
No matter which country you go to,

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:13.830
it looks like the people in power
there just love to build secret stuff.

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:16.870
Say, who exactly are you guys, anyway?

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:18.250
I told ya, didn't I?

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:21.040
We're champions of justice
that travel the world righting wrongs.

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:23.330
Champions of justice, huh?

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:25.790
Are ye siblings?

00:04:25.790 --> 00:04:29.950
Nope. Iris and I were involved in gangs,

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:33.040
but we each turned over
a new leaf after we met Tom.

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:38.160
He gave us a chance when we were
about to cross a line we shouldn't cross.

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:42.040
Tom showed us many different worlds.

00:04:42.910 --> 00:04:45.870
Poor, developing countries.

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:48.620
Children who had lost their parents
through acts of terrorism.

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:51.120
Children going hungry as a result of civil war.

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:54.750
And the lives of the ridiculously wealthy, too.

00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:58.250
There were lots of different
values swirling about the world.

00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:04.790
In the midst of that, Tom taught us how
to face the world and fight for freedom.

00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:10.540
What are "those children" of which
Ichijiku Kadenokoji hath spoken?

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:14.580
They're kids in a refugee camp
in a developing country.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:17.450
And they have been taken hostage?

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:18.660
Well...

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:21.330
Don't say more than you have to.

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:25.580
Our own circumstances have nothing to do
with the serious battle that's coming up.

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:29.790
It appears we've arrived.

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:45.870
Those mofos!

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:49.040
There's no way you can fight in your condition.

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:51.750
We, too, shall offer our assistance.

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:54.660
Hmph! Who asked for your help?

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:58.580
I can take those guys on single-handed.

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:01.750
It appears we don't have
the luxury of arguing over it.

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:03.160
Huh?!

00:06:07.330 --> 00:06:10.040
Yoo-hoo! Ichiro! Samatoki!

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:11.450
Oh!

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:12.750
Don't overdo it.

00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:17.080
Right now, we ain't got
the strength to move right.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:20.200
Huh?

00:06:20.870 --> 00:06:23.290
You guys are free to go.

00:06:24.910 --> 00:06:26.750
You're giving them back to us?

00:06:26.750 --> 00:06:28.700
That's so nice of you!

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:38.870
I hope none of you were hurt.

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:40.700
Same to you, Jakurai.

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:43.120
I'm sorry about what happened
to you because of us.

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:44.750
S'all good, man.

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:47.410
Life's a crapshoot, you know.

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:52.160
Only three of them came.

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:54.950
Well, there's nothing we can do about that.

00:06:54.950 --> 00:06:56.790
Tom...

00:06:56.790 --> 00:06:59.540
You will be fighting us.

00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:02.500
Hey, I told ya I could
take 'em on single-handed!

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:05.500
C'mon guys, would ya count
me in for old times' sake?

00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:08.950
With me in the mix, we'd have
ourselves a little Dirty Dawg reunion!

00:07:08.950 --> 00:07:10.950
I don't need no one's help, you fuckin' moron!

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:13.290
Don't say that, Samatoki!

00:07:13.290 --> 00:07:15.620
Those guys are like super tough, right?

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:19.200
Samatoki, if we don't fight them seriously,
we'll get our asses kicked.

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:22.500
That's Samatoki, <i>sir </i>to you!
You stinkin' sack of shit!

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:25.160
Tsk! Guess I got no choice!

00:07:25.160 --> 00:07:26.500
Yippee!

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:30.160
The legendary Dirty Dawg reunites!

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:32.830
Ramuda, are you guys gonna be okay?

00:07:32.830 --> 00:07:34.370
We'll be fine!

00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:38.950
You two watch us carefully and
burn our performance into your memory!

00:07:38.950 --> 00:07:42.330
Very well. We shall leave
this matter in your hands.

00:07:42.330 --> 00:07:46.160
You're gonna show us
what true legends are made of.

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:57.000
Tom.

00:07:57.000 --> 00:08:00.660
Was getting all chummy
with me also part of your scheme?

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:02.120
Ichiro....

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:04.160
I swear to you that's not the case.

00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:08.250
I respect you as a person
from the bottom of my heart.

00:08:08.910 --> 00:08:11.790
We accept your challenge!

00:08:11.790 --> 00:08:13.830
Look out for us, bastards!

00:08:13.830 --> 00:08:15.620
Here we come!

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:17.750
Everyone's groovin'!

00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:29.160
You guys get the first attack.

00:08:30.790 --> 00:08:32.410
They must realize that if
they concede the first attack,

00:08:32.410 --> 00:08:37.410
Jakurai Jinguji will use
his health recovery skill.

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:40.450
That's just how they are, I guess.

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:42.910
♬ The scattered heroes rally
Leave behind your melancholy ♬

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:45.450
♬ Both fate and chance, perhaps the first and last ♬

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:47.950
♬ No need to even ask,
we're ready for any battle forecast ♬

00:08:47.950 --> 00:08:50.410
♬ We got thousands of words
that form the winds in our mast ♬

00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:53.000
♬ Even more unreasonable than Chuohku ♬

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:55.330
♬ Take from us and we will
resist you with all we've got ♬

00:08:55.330 --> 00:08:57.910
♬ Fear not
Lighting only strikes at the very top ♬

00:08:57.910 --> 00:09:01.040
♬ Soon we'll obtain their anatomical plot ♬

00:09:07.410 --> 00:09:09.410
Looks like they've recovered.

00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:11.790
Now we can fight without pulling any punches!

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:16.410
♬ The Dirty Dawg?
Never heard of you, sweetie ♬

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:19.120
♬ Honestly, I don't know much
about ancient history ♬

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:21.790
♬ You're old, repetitive and hackneyed
A complete geezer, evidently ♬

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:24.200
♬ Stop acting like
this is a retirement home, geez ♬

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:26.790
♬ Your friendship is only temporary ♬

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:29.250
♬ Tom is the true icon, we are family ♬

00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:31.700
♬ Rex and I are the warding talismans ♬

00:09:31.700 --> 00:09:34.910
♬ It's my turn to protect them ♬

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:44.950
So, her rap bumps their skills up a notch...

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:48.620
Then, I'd better finish
'em off pretty damn quick!

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:51.620
♬ Yo' slowass cognitive
system's in constant strain ♬

00:09:51.620 --> 00:09:54.330
♬ Can't even register our freshness in your brain ♬

00:09:54.330 --> 00:09:56.660
♬ In the end these battles are like a food chain ♬

00:09:56.660 --> 00:09:59.370
♬ At the top you'll eat poison without the pain ♬

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:01.620
♬ Progressing evolution
Deepening excavation ♬

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:04.330
♬ Our true worth built
through trial and tribulation ♬

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:06.910
♬ Compared to me
You guys are nervous trainees ♬

00:10:06.910 --> 00:10:09.830
♬ On the edge of the abyss
You'll soon regret this ♬

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:21.580
Impressive!

00:10:21.580 --> 00:10:24.580
We would've been up a creek
if Iris hadn't protected us.

00:10:24.580 --> 00:10:28.620
Still, powerful foes get me
fired up that much more!

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:35.080
They awaken my DNA from
its 65-million-year slumber!

00:10:35.080 --> 00:10:36.910
♬ Top of the ecosystem, can't be beat ♬

00:10:36.910 --> 00:10:38.160
♬ Tyrannosaurus ♬

00:10:38.160 --> 00:10:40.500
♬ Favorite food is fresh meat ♬

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:43.160
♬ I'll bite through even those who got some spine ♬

00:10:43.160 --> 00:10:45.450
♬ Once I've got my eyes on you, you're mine ♬

00:10:45.450 --> 00:10:48.160
♬ Roooooaaar
I'm carnivore supreme ♬

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:50.450
♬ This hunt is just a murder scene ♬

00:10:50.450 --> 00:10:51.790
♬ The bigger the better ♬

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:53.000
♬ Dinosaur extreme ♬

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:56.120
♬ I'll never tire of the chase
Cretaceous Period great escape ♬

00:11:02.330 --> 00:11:05.830
Looks like we won't be able to
beat them unless we've got a game plan.

00:11:05.830 --> 00:11:09.200
Ichiro, lay down an attack
on the back of my rhymes!

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:12.290
♬ Yo! Gonna make you cheer
Oh, just plotting something top tier ♬

00:11:12.290 --> 00:11:14.250
♬ So says lil' ol' Ramu here
Yeah ♬

00:11:14.250 --> 00:11:16.750
♬ A rogue that'll take advantage
Of this emotional rollercoaster ♬

00:11:16.750 --> 00:11:19.200
♬ I've got a 100% success rate
I'm such a genius it's spooky! ♬

00:11:19.200 --> 00:11:22.370
♬ Check out how I juggle this verse
Fear Ramuda's unique lyrical style ♬

00:11:22.370 --> 00:11:24.250
♬ Gonna tear through your sinew ♬

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:26.700
♬ You're aliens?
Well we're enemies of the state ♬

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:30.120
♬ We're not the same, mate
When I've got a sense of justice innate ♬

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:35.660
Just what you'd expect from true legends.

00:11:35.660 --> 00:11:39.160
It appears I've finally found
an opponent that I can go all out against.

00:11:39.160 --> 00:11:42.040
So, you're saying you haven't gone all out yet?!

00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:46.330
I'll show you what it's like
when I go all out, Ichiro.

00:11:46.330 --> 00:11:49.410
♬ Develop and crop my lyrical architecture ♬

00:11:49.410 --> 00:11:51.450
♬ If you're boring you won't be remembered ♬

00:11:51.450 --> 00:11:53.950
♬ Doped up to the eyeballs, cells picking up steam ♬

00:11:53.950 --> 00:11:56.620
♬ If it wasn't for these pictures
they wouldn't find me at all ♬

00:11:56.620 --> 00:11:58.750
♬ To win the retreat, we all in to deep ♬

00:11:58.750 --> 00:12:01.660
♬ I'm in execution mode, TDD ♬

00:12:01.660 --> 00:12:04.290
♬ Think you're a frog in the well?
Nah, you're a big fish in the wrong pond ♬

00:12:04.290 --> 00:12:07.410
♬ Don't you get it?
This twisted rap show? ♬

00:12:18.410 --> 00:12:20.160
Clones?!

00:12:20.160 --> 00:12:24.120
No, it's a kaleidoscope reflecting them!

00:12:31.330 --> 00:12:33.870
So, they'll use this to amplify their attack?!

00:12:33.870 --> 00:12:36.870
What a tight spot we've been put in...

00:12:36.870 --> 00:12:39.620
To see the four of them
put under so much pressure!

00:12:39.620 --> 00:12:44.750
Having fought all over the world,
those guy's lyrics sure do pack a punch.

00:12:44.750 --> 00:12:46.290
You said it.

00:12:46.290 --> 00:12:53.500
The power of rap lies in how amazing
your life is and how much love you put into it.

00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:57.000
Now we'll put an end to this!

00:12:57.000 --> 00:12:58.500
Not so fast!

00:13:09.410 --> 00:13:11.120
Jiro! Saburo!

00:13:11.120 --> 00:13:13.120
Doppo! Hifumi!

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:14.910
Jyuto! Rio!

00:13:14.910 --> 00:13:17.830
While it's nice to reunite with old comrades...

00:13:17.830 --> 00:13:20.950
...where would you be without us, Samatoki?

00:13:20.950 --> 00:13:23.910
Dr. Jakurai, while we may not be of much use...

00:13:23.910 --> 00:13:26.080
...we'll do our best to help you!

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:27.950
Big Bro, we wanna...

00:13:27.950 --> 00:13:31.830
...fight by your side, Brother Ichi!
That feeling hasn't changed a bit!

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:34.540
Looks like the odds've started
to change in our favor.

00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:35.950
Count us in, too!

00:13:35.950 --> 00:13:38.410
Why not?

00:13:38.410 --> 00:13:41.160
It seems the four teams
have joined forces against us.

00:13:41.160 --> 00:13:44.410
It don't matter how many there are!
We'll still scatter them all!

00:13:44.410 --> 00:13:46.660
They make worthy opponents.

00:13:50.040 --> 00:13:51.290
C'mon guys!

00:13:51.290 --> 00:13:58.200
Hit 'em with everything you've got!

00:13:58.200 --> 00:13:59.250
♬ Psychological Judgments ♬

00:13:59.250 --> 00:14:01.660
♬ Shut up
You absurd ape ♬

00:14:01.660 --> 00:14:04.540
♬ Give you several degrees of payback
You, I'll personally smack ♬

00:14:04.540 --> 00:14:06.160
♬ How you been doing?
A sympathizer only focused on one thing ♬

00:14:06.160 --> 00:14:07.700
♬ Can you keep in step with this procession?
With our progression ♬

00:14:07.700 --> 00:14:10.370
♬ Doing my duty with some digression
You won't make my work go to waste, will you? ♬

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:12.160
--♬ Chain Gang ♬
--♬ Ah, I'm so friggin' bored ♬

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:13.790
♬ Wheezy inhale exhale
Then turnin' tail ♬

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:15.160
♬ Well, whatever
I'll let you go ♬

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:16.660
♬ So 1,000,000 yen
for protection fees is what you owe ♬

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:18.040
♬ Some hush money in my hand ♬

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:19.580
♬ Do you understand?
Don't ignore this demand ♬

00:14:19.580 --> 00:14:20.790
♬ Scouting out power is too absolute ♬

00:14:20.790 --> 00:14:22.250
♬ I'd quit if I were you
At best it's a jump with no parachute ♬

00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:25.660
--♬ Falsehood ♬
--♬ The talk from before that had no deceit ♬

00:14:25.660 --> 00:14:28.660
♬ Had no ground to stand on, and had to retreat
And we're now in nasty times, you see ♬

00:14:28.660 --> 00:14:31.700
♬ Far and wide a rainmaking voice
I cover my ears to silence the noise (oh well) ♬

00:14:31.700 --> 00:14:33.160
♬ Even if you put a lid
on something tricky temporarily ♬

00:14:33.160 --> 00:14:34.410
♬ Resounding in your mind is a siren ♬

00:14:34.410 --> 00:14:38.410
--♬ Till dawn ♬
--♬ All creation deserves death's embrace
There is dignity in disgrace ♬

00:14:38.410 --> 00:14:40.700
♬ Rhymes are an almighty poison which desecrates ♬

00:14:40.700 --> 00:14:42.160
♬ Bioluminescence
Withdraw their presence ♬

00:14:42.160 --> 00:14:43.700
♬ And this neon white night
Invites and heals ♬

00:14:43.700 --> 00:14:45.200
♬ Fighting through thin and thick
Conflict ♬

00:14:45.200 --> 00:14:48.200
♬ Conquer in a test of endurance
Concrete wall broken ♬

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:53.660
♬ Hypnosis action ends corruption ♬

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:55.870
♬ Gimmicks that will fry your synapses ♬

00:14:55.870 --> 00:15:01.950
♬ No one can stop this ignition! ♬

00:15:01.950 --> 00:15:05.750
♬ Now come to catharsis ♬

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:07.870
♬ Trample this rhyme ♬

00:15:07.870 --> 00:15:10.450
♬ Carve it into history ♬

00:15:10.450 --> 00:15:15.750
♬ at the Division Rap Battle ♬

00:15:18.830 --> 00:15:20.370
What <i>is </i>this?

00:15:20.370 --> 00:15:23.580
Their power--it's resonating?!

00:15:24.160 --> 00:15:26.870
What kind of power <i>is </i>this?!

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:43.450
To think we'd actually lose!

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:48.330
How d'ya like that!
This is the power of our rap!

00:15:48.330 --> 00:15:53.160
When it comes to living for the moment,
we can't be beat!

00:15:53.160 --> 00:15:58.790
To be sure, since you've seen the world,
you've got us beat in terms of experience.

00:15:58.790 --> 00:16:03.790
But Tom, you've forgotten
something very important.

00:16:03.790 --> 00:16:05.580
Something important?

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:10.410
Rapping is fun.

00:16:10.410 --> 00:16:12.910
So that explains it.

00:16:12.910 --> 00:16:15.370
The capacity to enjoy rapping...

00:16:15.370 --> 00:16:19.870
I was able to teach you
that rapping is a weapon to fight with.

00:16:19.870 --> 00:16:23.660
But I wasn't able to teach you
the capacity to enjoy it.

00:16:23.660 --> 00:16:25.160
Tom...

00:16:25.160 --> 00:16:30.330
It seemeth that imagination
hath bested experience in this bout.

00:16:30.330 --> 00:16:33.160
I'd just about had more than I could take!

00:16:33.160 --> 00:16:37.700
Now we can finally get away
from the Party of Words!

00:16:49.950 --> 00:16:51.250
The Party of Words!

00:16:51.250 --> 00:16:54.750
There's no way we can take on
that many of them now.

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:03.700
Secret Aliens.

00:17:03.700 --> 00:17:07.080
How dare you betray my expectations!

00:17:07.080 --> 00:17:12.250
Unfortunately for you,
our employer is not the Party of Words.

00:17:12.250 --> 00:17:20.330
No, we're not. Your employer is the man
who developed the hypnosis mic, isn't it?

00:17:23.160 --> 00:17:25.370
But it makes no difference.

00:17:25.370 --> 00:17:28.620
We'll make you just another part of our project.

00:17:28.620 --> 00:17:32.200
Seize them!

00:17:32.200 --> 00:17:36.330
The Party of Words is holding
some children in a refugee camp hostage.

00:17:36.330 --> 00:17:40.080
They said they'd cut off aid from Japan
if Secret Aliens couldn't beat us.

00:17:40.080 --> 00:17:41.540
That's terrible!

00:17:41.540 --> 00:17:43.910
Sounds like the kind of stunt
those big shots would pull!

00:17:43.910 --> 00:17:45.700
Is it true, Tom?

00:17:47.790 --> 00:17:49.660
Can't we do something?

00:17:49.660 --> 00:17:51.500
--We can.
--Huh?

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:54.450
I've got this entire conversation
recorded on video.

00:17:54.450 --> 00:17:56.330
Any more meddling and I'll stream this

00:17:56.330 --> 00:17:59.250
and show the world how
the Party of Words does things.

00:17:59.250 --> 00:18:00.830
Fine work, young man!

00:18:00.830 --> 00:18:02.500
Don't you make a fool of me!

00:18:02.500 --> 00:18:04.870
Still, do you really think you can do that?!

00:18:04.870 --> 00:18:06.580
Without the Party of Words,

00:18:06.580 --> 00:18:10.040
this country will once again be
sucked into the whirlpool of chaos!

00:18:10.040 --> 00:18:12.370
Do you really think things
would turn out that way?

00:18:12.370 --> 00:18:13.950
What did you say?

00:18:13.950 --> 00:18:17.660
We've taken a new step forward with our rapping.

00:18:17.660 --> 00:18:21.790
Whether you disappear or not,
the world will never go back to the way it was.

00:18:21.790 --> 00:18:24.290
Hmph! Ha ha ha ha!

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:27.200
The world is definitely
a shitty place right now.

00:18:27.200 --> 00:18:29.750
But at least we got <i>these </i>to fight it out with!

00:18:29.750 --> 00:18:35.040
Throughout the ages, a future of truth
has always been preferable to a false peace.

00:18:35.040 --> 00:18:37.750
And the truth is with <i>us</i>!

00:18:37.750 --> 00:18:39.000
OMG, did I just say that?

00:18:39.000 --> 00:18:42.000
You're telling me you men are the truth?

00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:45.120
You're merely slaves
to the bad old ways of thinking

00:18:45.120 --> 00:18:48.500
that built a world of foolish conflict!

00:18:48.500 --> 00:18:50.830
She's really, really pissed off.

00:18:50.830 --> 00:18:54.200
The way she is, it looks like even
<i>my </i>powers would have no effect on her.

00:18:54.200 --> 00:18:56.830
In this battle we don't stand a chance.

00:18:56.830 --> 00:19:00.290
She's got the hypnosis canceller
in her possession.

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:07.700
Return to me, Ichijiku.

00:19:07.700 --> 00:19:08.660
But...

00:19:08.660 --> 00:19:11.790
There is no need to pursue them
any further at this time.

00:19:15.660 --> 00:19:17.950
I can crush guys like you
whenever I feel like it.

00:19:17.950 --> 00:19:21.290
Just you wait. You'll get what's coming to you.

00:19:27.410 --> 00:19:29.950
It appears the crisis has passed, for now.

00:19:29.950 --> 00:19:31.540
Yeah.

00:19:36.450 --> 00:19:41.580
It appears that the four teams
have united thanks to your lapdogs.

00:19:41.580 --> 00:19:44.660
Eh-hehe. Sorry about that.

00:19:44.660 --> 00:19:50.410
But now's not the time to be risking a fight.

00:19:50.410 --> 00:19:53.750
Are you on our side?

00:19:53.750 --> 00:19:55.290
Or...

00:19:59.410 --> 00:20:02.540
Hmm, I could be.

00:20:03.790 --> 00:20:07.660
It appears we must put a new plan into action.

00:20:07.660 --> 00:20:09.200
Enter!

00:20:22.330 --> 00:20:27.200
Thou proposed to take us hostage
so that thou mightest rescue us.

00:20:27.200 --> 00:20:30.910
Thanks. You saved our necks back there.

00:20:30.910 --> 00:20:32.580
It's all in your head.

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:36.080
All I wanted to do was fight you guys.

00:20:36.080 --> 00:20:37.950
And you lost!

00:20:37.950 --> 00:20:39.160
Hey, now!

00:20:39.160 --> 00:20:41.160
Ichiro. Doctor.

00:20:41.160 --> 00:20:44.620
Thanks guys. I hope we get
the chance to meet each other again.

00:20:44.620 --> 00:20:48.040
By that time, we'll be even bigger.

00:20:48.040 --> 00:20:51.410
Then we'll be even bigger than that!

00:20:51.410 --> 00:20:56.080
--Later!
--Saburo Yamada, next time I see you,
the ramen's on me.

00:20:56.080 --> 00:20:58.410
Huh? What's she talking about?

00:21:03.660 --> 00:21:08.000
Well, I guess we also better be
gettin' back to our shitty daily lives.

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:10.120
Later, Doc. Ramuda.

00:21:10.120 --> 00:21:13.000
Huh? You three loser brothers
are still hangin' around?

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:15.200
--What?
--What'd you call us?

00:21:15.200 --> 00:21:18.330
What, Samatoki? You begging for a fight?

00:21:18.330 --> 00:21:22.660
Ichiro, Samatoki, for my sake, please don't--

00:21:22.660 --> 00:21:24.080
Doc.

00:21:24.080 --> 00:21:26.200
Just 'cause you beat us that one time,

00:21:26.200 --> 00:21:29.000
don't give you the right to act
all high and mighty.

00:21:29.000 --> 00:21:31.450
Are you saying our victory was a fluke?

00:21:31.450 --> 00:21:35.080
That was the result of our... our sheer talent!

00:21:35.080 --> 00:21:37.750
Doppo, Hifumi, don't get angry now.

00:21:37.750 --> 00:21:39.620
Shut up, you old coot!

00:21:39.620 --> 00:21:41.950
Things were just starting to get interesting!

00:21:41.950 --> 00:21:44.040
You're the one who had better "shut up."

00:21:44.040 --> 00:21:48.160
Hey, have you forgotten that
we're the ones who saved all of you?

00:21:48.160 --> 00:21:51.790
I find it surprising that you didn't
just run off and leave everyone behind.

00:21:51.790 --> 00:21:54.540
Want me to fight you again, you old coot?

00:21:54.540 --> 00:21:56.790
If it's a game that can get us
back on our feet again, I'm in.

00:21:56.790 --> 00:22:00.500
'Tis an opportunity for us
to return to the fray.

00:22:00.500 --> 00:22:04.660
Looks like everyone can't
get enough of a good fight.

00:22:04.660 --> 00:22:06.370
Everyone?

00:22:06.370 --> 00:22:10.160
The phrase "desertion in the face of the enemy"
does not appear in my dictionary.

00:22:10.160 --> 00:22:12.120
I should've known this would happen.

00:22:12.120 --> 00:22:14.790
All right, bring it on!

00:22:14.790 --> 00:22:17.080
Here we go!

00:22:17.080 --> 00:22:20.040
The party's still goin' strong!

00:22:20.040 --> 00:22:22.660
Let's fight!
